---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Game from '../../components/Game.tsx';
import { stats } from '../../lib/data';
import { u, pct } from '../../lib/fmt';
const s = stats();
const pl = s.predictors.p_le_005, pm = s.predictors.p_005_05;
---
<Base title="Did it replicate?" description="A calibration game: read a real psychology finding, say how likely it is that it replicated, and see what happened." active="game/">
  <div class="wrap gwrap">
    <header class="ghead rise">
      <div class="label claim">The game</div>
      <h1>Did it <em>replicate?</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Read a finding from a real psychology paper. Say how sure you are that later replications found the same thing. Then see what actually happened — in the replicators' own words.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="grid grid-main">
      <Game client:load base={u('')} />
      <noscript>
        <section class="card gnojs" aria-labelledby="gnojs-title">
          <div class="label">JavaScript needed for the game</div>
          <h2 id="gnojs-title">Browse the record instead</h2>
          <p>The game reveals each result only after a prediction, so it needs JavaScript. You can still explore the underlying record by <a href={u('effects/')}>browsing effects</a> or <a href={u('findings/')}>browsing papers</a>.</p>
        </section>
      </noscript>
      <aside class="ghints stack">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="label">What predicts a replication</div>
          <p>In this deck, originals with <b>p ≤ .005</b> replicated <b class="num">{pct(pl.success_share)}</b> of the time (n = {pl.n}); those with <b>.005 &lt; p &lt; .05</b> only <b class="num">{pct(pm.success_share)}</b> (n = {pm.n}).</p>
          <p>Across all {s.overall.n.toLocaleString()} replications with a verdict, <b class="num">{pct(s.overall.success_share)}</b> succeeded. Social psychology: <b class="num">{pct(s.by_discipline['Social Psychology']?.success_share)}</b>. Cognitive: <b class="num">{pct(s.by_discipline['Cognitive Psychology']?.success_share)}</b>.</p>
          <p class="faint gsmall">Base rates reflect which studies people chose to replicate, not psychology as a whole. <a href={u('stats/')}>More on the record</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="label">How the deck is built</div>
          <p style="font-size:.95rem">One card per original study, only where the replication verdict is clear and consistent. Claims that give the answer away are removed automatically. The daily round uses a fixed, quality-controlled mix. The result is fetched only after you lock in.</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .gwrap { padding-top: 2.4rem; }
  .ghead h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--claim); font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 100, "WONK" 1; }
  .lede { font: 400 1.25rem/1.5 var(--f-display); color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 60ch; }
  :global(.gmodes) { display: grid; gap: .8rem; }
  :global(.gm) { text-align: left; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--ink); border-radius: var(--r); padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem; cursor: pointer; color: var(--ink); font: inherit; transition: transform .15s, box-shadow .15s; }
  :global(.gm:hover) { transform: translate(-2px, -2px); box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--claim); }
  :global(.gm b) { display: block; font: 560 1.35rem var(--f-display); margin-bottom: .2rem; }
  :global(.gm span) { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .95rem; }
  :global(.gtop) { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--ink-3); margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  :global(.gcard) { min-height: 360px; }
  :global(.gname) { margin: .5rem 0 0; }
  :global(.gclaim) { font: 400 clamp(1.25rem, 2.4vw, 1.6rem)/1.4 var(--f-display); margin: .8rem 0 .5rem; }
  /* how the study was run, under the claim: the player needs it to judge, so it is quieter but not hidden */
  :global(.gmethod) { font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-2, #555); margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
  /* the provenance of an unreviewed card, in its reveal: it is not the record and must not read like it */
  :global(.gunver) { font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: .5rem 0 .8rem; padding: .6rem .8rem;
    border-left: 3px dashed var(--line, #ccc); color: var(--ink-2, #555); }
  :global(.gj) { font-size: .92rem; }
  :global(.gnums) { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .4rem 1.1rem; font-size: .82rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  :global(.gguess) { margin-top: 1.4rem; border-top: 1px dashed var(--rule-2); padding-top: 1.2rem; }
  :global(.gq) { font: 500 1.02rem var(--f-display); display: block; margin-bottom: .6rem; }
  :global(.gslider) { display: flex; gap: .7rem; align-items: center; }
  :global(.gslider input) { flex: 1; accent-color: var(--obs); height: 2.75rem; }
  :global(.gp) { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: .4rem 0 .9rem; }
  :global(.gp b) { font: 600 2rem var(--f-display); }
  :global(.gnote) { font-size: .8rem; margin-top: .8rem; }
  :global(.greveal) { margin-top: 1.3rem; border-top: 1px dashed var(--rule-2); padding-top: 1.2rem; }
  :global(.greveal .stamp) { font-size: .9rem; }
  :global(.gpts) { font: 600 1.6rem var(--f-display); margin: .8rem 0; }
  :global(.gpts span) { font: .8rem var(--f-mono); margin-left: .5rem; }
  :global(.grep) { margin-bottom: .8rem; }
  :global(.grep p) { font-size: .74rem; margin: 0 0 .3rem; }
  :global(.glinks) { font-size: .92rem; }
  :global(.gsum .big) { font: 600 2.6rem var(--f-display); margin: .3rem 0; }
  :global(.gsum .emo) { font-size: 1.5rem; letter-spacing: .1em; }
  :global(.gsum) { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  :global(.gcal) { margin-top: 1rem; }
  :global(.gcal svg) { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; max-width: 320px; }
  :global(.gcal svg text) { font-family: var(--f-mono); font-size: 9px; fill: var(--ink-3); }
  .gnojs { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .gnojs h2 { margin-top: .35rem; }
  .gsmall { font-size: .85rem; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .gwrap { padding-top: 1.5rem; }
    .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; }
    :global(.gcard) { min-height: 0; }
    :global(.gm) { min-height: 44px; padding: 1rem; }
    :global(.gslider) { gap: .45rem; }
    :global(.gslider input) { min-width: 0; }
    :global(.gcal) { overflow: hidden; }
    .gsmall { font-size: .9rem; }
  }
</style>
